Qualifications



To apply for the CHED Merit Scholarship Program (CMSP), students must meet the following qualifications:




Must be a Filipino citizen; 



Must be a graduate of a Senior High School in the Philippines with a minimum General Average (GA) or General Weighted Average (GWA) of 93% or its equivalent; 



Must have parents or legal guardians with a combined annual gross income not exceeding ₱500,000; 



Must obtain admission in any of the following Higher Education Institutions:

State Universities and Colleges (SUCs);



Local Universities and Colleges (LUCs) with Institutional Recognition (IR); or



CHED-recognized Private Higher Education Institutions (PHEIs);





Must enroll in a CHED-identified priority program offered by:

PHEIs with Government Recognition;



SUCs with Certificate of Program Compliance (COPC); or



LUCs with COPC.

