Qualifications



To qualify for the CHED EASE Scholarship Program, applicants must meet the following qualifications:




Must be a Filipino citizen residing in the Philippines;



Must belong to any recognized Special Equity Group (SEG) and provide supporting certification;



Must be a graduate of Senior High School in the Philippines with a minimum general average of at least 85% or its equivalent;



Must be an incoming or current first-year Filipino college student for Academic Year 2026-2027;



Must be admitted or enrolled in a CHED-recognized or certified priority undergraduate program; and



Must have an individual income, if employed, or combined annual gross income of parents or legal guardians that does not exceed ₱2,000,000.

